cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Processing- and cell-stage thermodynamic screening of nacre- and bone-inspired carbonate and phosphate phases on aluminium current collectors in fluorine-free lithium-ion cells with an open screening framework"
abstract: "An open framework that screens candidate mineral coatings, biopolymer-templated carbonate and phosphate phases, against two thermodynamic tests: dissolution in the alkaline aqueous slurry of electrode processing, and the oxidation onset at the aluminium current collector of a lithium-ion cell. Inputs are sourced thermochemistry with propagated uncertainty; outputs are stage-resolved exclusion maps, break-even ratios, required-precision maps and the input value at which each verdict flips. The repository re-derives every number, table and data figure of the accompanying paper from the sourced parameter file and cached inputs. It does not test any coating experimentally."
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pa1aash/biomin-screen"
keywords:
  - thermodynamic screening
  - biomimetic mineralisation
  - biopolymer-templated carbonate
  - biopolymer-templated phosphate
  - calcium carbonate
  - calcium phosphate
  - aluminium current collector
  - lithium-ion cathode coating
  - Pourbaix diagram
  - uncertainty propagation
